      "exam": "exam-ok",
      "notes": "=== KEY OUTPUT FIELDS ===\n  DNSRoot              → INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL (FQDN)\n  NetBIOSName          → INLANEFREIGHT (short name for older authentication)\n  DomainSID            → S-1-5-21-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX (domain SID — critical for attacks)\n  Forest               → INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL (forest root — same if no parent)\n  ChildDomains         → {LOGISTICS.INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL}\n  ParentDomain         → (empty if this IS the forest root)\n  DomainMode           → Windows2016Domain (functional level)\n  PDCEmulator          → ACADEMY-EA-DC01.INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL (FSMO role)\n\n=== WHY THE DOMAIN SID MATTERS ===\nThe domain SID is required for:\n  - Building golden tickets (krbtgt hash + SID → golden ticket)\n  - ExtraSids attack (child SID + parent Enterprise Admins SID → cross-domain)\n  - Enumeration of RID-based accounts (Administrator = SID + RID 500)\n\nTo get child domain SID from parent domain:\n  Get-ADDomain -Identity LOGISTICS.INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL | select DomainSID\n\n=== FSMO ROLES ===\nGet-ADDomain shows: PDCEmulator, RIDMaster, InfrastructureMaster\nGet-ADForest shows: SchemaMaster, DomainNamingMaster\nDC with PDCEmulator is highest-value target — it handles password changes,\ntime sync, and lockout policy. If you compromise it, you own the domain.\n\n=== ALTERNATIVE — POWERVIEW ===\nGet-Domain (PowerView equivalent)\nGet-DomainSID (returns just the SID)",
