      "defense": {
        "prerequisites": "Adobe ColdFusion 8.0.1 or earlier with the bundled FCKeditor package present and reachable at /CFIDE/scripts/ajax/FCKeditor/. No authentication required.",
        "why_it_works": "The FCKeditor connector's FileUpload command does not authenticate the caller or validate the uploaded file type/extension, so a .jsp payload can be written into a web-served directory and then executed by requesting it.",
        "misconfiguration": "Unpatched CF8 exposing the FCKeditor file manager to unauthenticated users; upload directory (/userfiles/) is web-executable.",
        "impact": "Unauthenticated remote code execution as the ColdFusion service account - commonly SYSTEM on Windows, i.e. full host compromise.",
        "detection": "Web log: POST to .../FCKeditor/editor/filemanager/connectors/cfm/upload.cfm?Command=FileUpload; creation of .jsp files under /userfiles/file/; subsequent GET to a random-named .jsp; unexpected outbound connection from the CF host (reverse shell).",
        "artifacts": "Dropped .jsp payload in the CF webroot/userfiles; FCKeditor upload entries in access logs; new child processes spawned by the ColdFusion/JRun process.",
        "vulnerable_config": "# ColdFusion 8.0.1, FCKeditor connector reachable pre-auth\n# /CFIDE/scripts/ajax/FCKeditor/.../upload.cfm accepts .jsp",
        "secure_config": "# Apply Adobe hotfix for CVE-2009-2265; remove the bundled FCKeditor\n# Block/remove /CFIDE/scripts/ajax/FCKeditor if unused\n# Deny script execution in upload directories; run CF as least-privilege",
        "prevention": "Patch CVE-2009-2265 and remove the vulnerable FCKeditor. Disable execution in upload directories. Restrict /CFIDE/ to internal IPs. Run ColdFusion as a non-privileged service account, not SYSTEM. [MITRE M1051, M1042, M1026]",
        "evasion": "Randomized payload filenames evade static IOC lists; upload then immediately delete the payload after the shell connects (the script does this) to reduce on-disk artifacts.",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M24",
          "MITRE T1190",
          "MITRE T1505.003",
          "CVE-2009-2265"
        ],
        "code_review": "RED FLAGS (source): file saved using client-supplied name/extension; MIME trusted from the request.\n  move_uploaded_file(..., $_FILES['f']['name'])  |  extension blacklist  |  type check on $_FILES['f']['type'] (client-controlled)\nGREP:  grep -rniE \"move_uploaded_file|\\$_FILES|multer|formidable|MultipartFile|SaveAs\\(\" .\nSAFE:  extension ALLOWLIST + magic-byte MIME (finfo/mime_content_type), server-generated random filename, store outside webroot in a no-execute dir."
      }
