        "secure_config": "# PHP — avoid shell entirely; use native functions:\n// Instead of: system('ping -c 1 ' . $ip)\n// Use: socket-based ping via fsockopen() or ICMP raw socket\n// If shell unavoidable, use escapeshellarg():\n$ip = escapeshellarg($_GET['ip']);\nsystem('ping -c 1 ' . $ip);\n// escapeshellarg() wraps input in single quotes and escapes internal quotes\n\n// Even better — strict allowlist validation first:\nif (!filter_var($_GET['ip'], FILTER_VALIDATE_IP)) {\n    die('Invalid IP address');\n}\n\n# NodeJS — use array form (no shell interpretation):\nconst { execFile } = require('child_process');\nexecFile('ping', ['-c', '1', userIP], callback);\n// execFile with array args never invokes a shell\n\n# Python — list form:\nsubprocess.run(['ping', '-c', '1', user_ip])  # No shell=True\n\n# PHP config — disable dangerous functions:\n; php.ini\ndisable_functions = system,exec,shell_exec,passthru,popen,proc_open\nopen_basedir = /var/www/html\n\n# WAF: ModSecurity, Cloudflare — block ; && | operators in parameters",
        "prevention": "Never pass user input to shell functions — use language-native equivalents (fsockopen instead of ping, DNS libraries instead of nslookup). If unavoidable: escapeshellarg() / escapeshellcmd(). Strict allowlist input validation (FILTER_VALIDATE_IP for IP fields, regex for structured inputs). disable_functions in php.ini. Least-privilege web server account. WAF with command injection signatures.",
