      "notes": "=== SHARES OUTPUT ===\n  Share          Permissions  Remark\n  -----          -----------  ------\n  ADMIN$         NO ACCESS    Remote Admin\n  C$             NO ACCESS    Default Share\n  Department Shares READ       \n  IPC$           READ\n  NETLOGON       READ         Logon server share\n  SYSVOL         READ         Logon server share\n  user_share     READ, WRITE  User files\n\n=== WHAT'S INTERESTING ===\n  Non-default shares     → Department Shares, user_share, IT, Finance\n  READ access            → explore contents for credentials, configs\n  WRITE access           → drop SCF/LNK files to capture hashes, or plant payloads\n  SYSVOL                 → always explore for GPP passwords and logon scripts\n\n=== WRITE ACCESS ATTACK ===\nIf you have WRITE to a share: place a malicious SCF/LNK file.\nWhen a user browses the share, Windows auto-sends NTLM auth to the attacker.\nUse Responder to capture the NTLMv2 hash.\n\n=== SPIDER CONTENTS ===\ncrackmapexec smb <dc> -u user -p pass -M spider_plus -o READ_ONLY=False\n→ Spiders all accessible share content",
