      "exam": "exam-ok",
      "notes": "=== WHAT TO LOOK FOR IN OUTPUT ===\n  [+] Dumping password info for domain: INLANEFREIGHT\n  Minimum password length: 8\n  Password history length: 24\n  Maximum password age: Not Set\n  Password Complexity Flags: Domain Passwords Complex: 1\n  Bad password lockout threshold: 5\n  Reset Account Lockout Counter: 30 minutes\n  Locked Account Duration: 30 minutes\n  Account Lockout Threshold: 5\n\nCritical numbers:\n  Account Lockout Threshold = 5  → spray max 3 attempts (stay 2 below)\n  Reset Account Lockout Counter = 30 min → wait 30 min between spray rounds\n\n=== SPRAY MATH ===\nThreshold = 5\nSafe spray count = threshold - 2 = 3 attempts per user\nWait between rounds = Reset Counter value (30 min in this example)\nSpray 3 passwords → wait 30+ min → spray 3 more → etc.\n\n=== IF THRESHOLD = 0 ===\n'Account Lockout Threshold: 0' = no lockout policy\nYou can spray freely without lockout risk.\nStill generates 4625 events on each failed attempt.\n\n=== ALTERNATIVE METHODS ===\nWindowds: net accounts /domain\nPowerView: Get-DomainPasswordPolicy\nenum4linux-ng: -P flag",
