        "why_it_works": "GraphQL exposes a typed schema where clients specify exactly what data they want. Introspection queries reveal all types, fields, mutations, and relationships — giving attackers a complete API map without any documentation. Mutations can modify data. Batching (sending arrays of queries) multiplies attack throughput. IDOR occurs when object references in query arguments are not authorization-checked server-side.",
