      "defense": {
        "prerequisites": "An IDOR vulnerability exists on an API endpoint. Mass enumeration is required to find specific records (admin accounts, flagged data).",
        "why_it_works": "bash + curl + grep provides a lightweight enumeration pipeline: loop over integer UIDs, curl fetches each API response, grep filters for target patterns (admin, specific role, email domain). This is faster than manual Burp Intruder for simple enumeration. Bash scripting also handles POST-based IDOR and custom headers.",
        "misconfiguration": "API exposes all user records via sequential UID with no authorization. No rate limiting.",
        "impact": "Automated discovery of admin accounts, privileged users, and specific data records across the full user database.",
        "detection": "[MITRE T1083] Rate limiting: high-frequency sequential requests from single session. Access log: user agent pattern (curl/7.x from automated script). SIEM: API enumeration pattern.",
        "artifacts": "Access log: sequential API requests with curl User-Agent. API: all user records accessed from single session in sequence.",
        "prevention": "Server-side authorization. Rate limiting (10 API requests/minute per session). Require explicit permission to query other users' records.",
        "vulnerable_config": "# No auth check on API:\nGET /api.php/user/1  -> returns any user's data\nGET /api.php/user/52 -> returns admin's data",
        "secure_config": "# Return only session user's own record:\nGET /api.php/user/  -> returns $_SESSION['uid'] user's data only\n# Admin can query others, non-admin cannot",
        "evasion": "for uid in {1..100}; do curl -s /api/user/$uid; echo; done | grep admin",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M23",
          "MITRE T1083",
          "OWASP A01:2021"
        ],
        "code_review": "RED FLAGS (source): object fetched by a request-supplied id with NO ownership/authorization check.\n  SELECT * FROM x WHERE id = req.params.id   (no AND owner_id = session.user)  |  findById(req.query.id) returned directly\nGREP:  grep -rniE \"findById|WHERE id ?= ?(\\$_|req\\.|params)|/:(id|uid|user_id)\" .\nSAFE:  enforce OBJECT-LEVEL authorization on every access (verify the resource belongs to the caller); use unpredictable IDs (UUID) as defense-in-depth only."
      },
