        "prerequisites": "ADCS web enrollment over HTTP (no EPA), a coercion vector, and a relay host.",
        "impact": "A certificate for a privileged identity (often a DC) enabling PKINIT auth and DCSync - domain compromise.",
        "detection": "[MITRE T1649] Certificate-based Kerberos auth (PKINIT): 4768 with a certificate; on the CA, 4886/4887 certificate requests where the SAN != requester; abnormal certificate issuance; ntlmrelay to ADCS shows a relayed request from a non-DC IP. On the CA, a DomainController-template request sourced from the relay IP rather than the DC.",
        "artifacts": "A relayed cert request (4886/4887 from the relay IP); the issued cert; coercion + relay traffic.",
        "prevention": "Enforce HTTPS + Extended Protection for Authentication on ADCS web enrollment; disable it if unused; block coercion (patch/disable Spooler); Harden ADCS templates (remove ENROLLEE_SUPPLIES_SUBJECT, require manager approval, restrict enrollment); enforce HTTPS + Extended Protection on web enrollment (ESC8); monitor 4886/4887 and PKINIT logons; restrict who can enroll.",
