      "id": "ad-kerbrute-userenum",
      "name": "Kerbrute - Username Enumeration via Kerberos",
      "command": "kerbrute userenum -d <domain> --dc <dc_ip> <userlist> -o valid_users.txt",
      "description": "Validates usernames against a domain using Kerberos pre-authentication requests. The KDC returns different responses for valid vs invalid users (PRINCIPAL_UNKNOWN vs PREAUTH_REQUIRED or PREAUTH_FAILED). No lockouts triggered — this tests existence, not passwords. Output valid users to file for spray operations.",
      "platform": "linux",
      "type": "command",
      "opsec": "moderate",
      "category": "Enumeration",
      "subcategory": "AD Enumeration",
      "certifications": [
        "CPTS",
        "OSCP"
      ],
      "primary_cert": "CPTS",
      "source": "CPTS Module 13: Active Directory Enumeration & Attacks",
      "tags": [
        "kerbrute",
        "username-enumeration",
        "kerberos",
        "user-validation"
      ],
      "mitre": [
        "T1087.002"
      ],
      "exam": "exam-ok",
      "notes": "=== HOW KERBEROS USERNAME VALIDATION WORKS ===\nKerbrute sends Kerberos AS-REQ packets for each username being tested.\nThe KDC's response reveals account existence:\n  KDC_ERR_C_PRINCIPAL_UNKNOWN  → account does NOT exist\n  KDC_ERR_PREAUTH_REQUIRED     → account EXISTS (pre-auth required)\n  KDC_ERR_PREAUTH_FAILED       → account EXISTS (wrong password but valid user)\n\nNo password is used — just username probing via Kerberos error codes.\nThis does NOT trigger account lockouts because no authentication attempt fails.\n\n=== NO LOCKOUT — BUT STILL DETECTABLE ===\nWhile userenum doesn't trigger lockouts, it does generate Event 4768\n(Kerberos TGT request) on the DC for each request.\nMany requests for unknown users in rapid succession is detectable by:\n  - Microsoft Defender for Identity\n  - SIEM rules watching 4768 error rates\nSlow it down with --delay if needed.\n\n=== OUTPUT ===\n  [+] VALID USERNAME: jsmith@INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL\n  [+] VALID USERNAME: htb-student@INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL\n  2024/01/01 12:00:00 >  Done! Tested 89 usernames (56 valid) in 0.920 seconds\n\n=== BUILD USER LIST FROM ===\n  Username-Anarchy from OSINT names → generate\n  /usr/share/seclists/Usernames/Names/names.txt → generic list\n  OSINT: LinkedIn, company website\n  Previous breach data\n\n=== CHAIN ===\n  userenum → valid_users.txt → passwordspray with kerbrute → valid creds",
      "examples": [
        {
          "label": "Enum against a wordlist",
          "command": "kerbrute userenum -d INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL --dc 172.16.5.5 /opt/jsmith.txt -o valid_ad_users"
        },
        {
          "label": "Enum generated names",
          "command": "kerbrute userenum -d INLANEFREIGHT.LOCAL --dc 172.16.5.5 generated_usernames.txt -o valid_users.txt"
        }
      ],
