        "vulnerable_config": "# Anonymous LDAP bind allowed (old domain or misconfigured):\n# Test: ldapsearch -H ldap://<dc> -x -b '' -s base  (no -D or -w)\n# If returns results -> anonymous bind works\n\n# AD attribute exposure to all authenticated users (default permissive ACL):\n# All users can read: userPrincipalName, sAMAccountName, memberOf,\n#   servicePrincipalName, description, pwdLastSet, adminCount\n# Description field often contains passwords set by admins during provisioning",
        "secure_config": "# Disable LDAP anonymous binds on domain controllers:\n# Registry (on each DC):\nSet-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\NTDS\\Parameters' \\\n    -Name 'LDAPServerIntegrity' -Value 2  # require signing\n\n# Force LDAPS (LDAP over TLS) — block plaintext LDAP:\n# GPO: Domain Controller Security Policy\n#   Network Security: LDAP client signing requirements = Require signing\n\n# Audit AD attribute ACLs — check who can read sensitive attributes:\nGet-ADObject (Get-ADDomain).DistinguishedName -Properties nTSecurityDescriptor\n\n# Remove passwords from description/info fields (audit quarterly):\nGet-ADUser -Filter * -Properties Description |\n    Where-Object {$_.Description -match 'pass|pwd|password|temp'} |\n    Select-Object SamAccountName, Description\n\n# Enable LDAP channel binding (KB4520412):\n# HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\NTDS\\Parameters\n#   LdapEnforceChannelBinding = 2"
