      "notes": "Null byte fixed in PHP 5.5+. On PHP < 5.3/5.4 use path truncation instead: pad the path past the 4096-byte limit so the extension is dropped - generate with: echo -n \"nonexistent/../../../etc/passwd/\" && for i in {1..2048}; do echo -n \"./\"; done. Append the result as the parameter value. Also covered in: OSCP PEN-200 Chapter 9 (Common Web Application Attacks).",
