      "id": "msf-payload-types",
      "name": "Metasploit - Payload Types and Naming",
      "type": "cheatsheet",
      "command": "show payloads",
      "description": "How Metasploit payloads are named and the common ones. A single (inline) payload is self-contained; a staged payload splits a small stager that pulls the larger stage over the connection - shown by a slash in the name. Getting this right is what makes a multi/handler match a generated payload.",
