        "prerequisites": "netcat/ncat on the listening host and a reachable port between attacker and target.",
        "impact": "A channel that receives an interactive shell from the target.",
        "detection": "On the target side the tell is the outbound connection to the listener and the shell interpreter; the listener itself is attacker-side. nc/ncat execution shows in process logs.",
        "artifacts": "An nc/ncat listener process; the inbound shell connection; on the target, the outbound connection to this listener.",
        "prevention": "Egress filtering (restrict outbound ports/hosts) so a target cannot reach an arbitrary listener; IDS/IPS on raw shell traffic; EDR flagging nc/ncat.",
