      "notes": "NSE vuln scripts DETECT (and a few safely confirm) known flaws — they're allowed on the OSCP exam because they're part of nmap, unlike Nessus/OpenVAS which are prohibited. --script vuln runs every script tagged 'vuln'; it's noisy and some scripts actively probe, so scope to specific ports/services. To use a CVE script you downloaded, drop the .nse into /usr/share/nmap/scripts and run --script-updatedb so nmap indexes it. Cross-check hits against searchsploit before trusting them. Also covered in: OSCP PEN-200 Chapter 7 (Vulnerability Scanning).",
