      "notes": "A one-line PHP webshell (`<?php system($_GET['cmd']); ?>`) gives command exec via the browser. Trade it up to a real reverse shell fast - webshells are fragile and get cleaned. Watch for disable_functions/open_basedir. PHP webshells bypass upload filters by spoofing MIME type. Common upload paths: /images/vendor/, /uploads/, /files/. Minimal shell: <?php system($_GET['cmd']); ?> GET-based. Use URL encoding for special chars in cmd. wwwolf provides a GUI webshell. Also covered in: CPTS Ch08.",
