      "notes": "Config in /etc/proxychains.conf, e.g. 'socks4 127.0.0.1 9050' or 'socks5 127.0.0.1 1080'. Only TCP connect scans work through the proxy. Also covered in: OSCP PEN-200 Chapter 18 (Port Redirection and SSH Tunneling). OSCP Ch18: socks5 in proxychains4.conf is required for SSH -D (not socks4). nmap MUST use -sT (TCP connect) through proxychains — raw SYN (-sS) and UDP scans do not traverse SOCKS proxies. -Pn skips the ping phase (ICMP also doesn't tunnel).",
