      "mitre": [
        "T1190",
        "T1136.001"
      ],
      "exam": "exam-ok",
      "defense": {
        "why_it_works": "PRTG's notification system allows admins to execute programs when alerts fire. The parameter field for the EXE/script notification is unsanitized, enabling OS command injection via semicolons appended after the filename.",
        "prerequisites": "Valid PRTG admin credentials (default prtgadmin:prtgadmin often unchanged). Access to PRTG web interface. Ability to create/modify notifications and trigger them.",
        "impact": "OS command execution as PRTG service account (often SYSTEM on Windows). Can create local admin users, install backdoors, run Mimikatz -- full Windows host compromise.",
        "detection": "PRTG notification creation or modification. Unusual child process from PRTGServer.exe (net.exe, whoami.exe). Windows Security Event 4688 for process creation from PRTG. New local admin account (4720/4732).",
        "artifacts": "PRTG audit log (notification modified) | Windows Security Event 4688 (net.exe from PRTG) | Windows Event 4720/4732 (new admin user) | EDR: PRTG spawning cmd.exe",
        "prevention": "Change default PRTG credentials immediately. Restrict PRTG web interface to internal IPs. Apply PRTG patches. Run PRTG service as a non-admin service account. Monitor for new local admin account creation.",
        "misconfiguration": "PRTG running with default credentials. Service runs as SYSTEM. Notification system allows semicolon-injected OS commands without sanitization.",
        "vulnerable_config": "# PRTG default\n# Service account: SYSTEM\n# Credentials: prtgadmin:prtgadmin\n# Notification param: 'test.txt;net user admin Pwn3d! /add'\n# No input sanitization",
        "secure_config": "# Change default credentials immediately\n# Run PRTG as low-privilege service account:\nNew-LocalUser -Name \"prtg_svc\" -Password (ConvertTo-SecureString \"StrongPass!\" -AsPlainText -Force)\n# Alert on Windows Event 4732 (member added to Administrators)",
        "evasion": "Trigger via legitimate alert threshold rather than Test button to avoid direct admin action in audit trail.",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M24",
          "MITRE T1190",
          "MITRE T1059",
          "OWASP A03:2021"
        ],
        "code_review": "RED FLAGS (source): user input reaches a shell/exec call.\n  system( / exec( / shell_exec( / passthru( / popen( / proc_open(  |  os.system / subprocess(..., shell=True)  |  child_process.exec(  |  backticks `...`\nGREP:  grep -rniE \"system\\(|exec\\(|shell_exec|passthru|popen|proc_open|os\\.system|subprocess.*shell=True|child_process\\.exec\\(|`.*\\$\" .\nSAFE:  avoid the shell; use argument arrays / execve-style APIs (subprocess.run([...], shell=False)); strict allowlist; escapeshellarg only as last resort."
      }
