      "notes": "=== Files of Interest Reference — Extended Credential and Sensitive Data Locations ===\nComprehensive checklist of high-value file locations to check during post-exploitation.\n\n=== HIGH-VALUE REGISTRY HIVE COPIES ===\nC:\\Windows\\repair\\SAM              → backup SAM hive (local account hashes)\nC:\\Windows\\repair\\SYSTEM           → needed to decrypt SAM\nC:\\Windows\\system32\\config\\SAM    → live (locked) - access via VSS or SeBackupPrivilege\nC:\\Windows\\system32\\config\\SYSTEM → live (locked) - same\nC:\\Windows\\system32\\config\\*.sav  → .sav extension = backup copies from Windows Setup\n\n=== LOG AND CONFIG FILES ===\n%WINDIR%\\System32\\CCM\\logs\\*.log          → SCCM deployment logs (may contain credentials)\n%WINDIR%\\System32\\drivers\\etc\\hosts       → internal DNS names / network topology\nC:\\inetpub\\wwwroot\\web.config             → IIS connection strings\nC:\\inetpub\\wwwroot\\*\\appsettings.json    → .NET Core connection strings\n*.rdp files anywhere                         → saved RDP sessions with encoded credentials\n*.vnc files                                  → VNC password configuration\n*.config files                               → application configuration\nNetSetup.log                                 → domain join credentials\n\n=== VIRTUAL DISK AND BACKUP FILES ===\n*.vhd, *.vhdx files               → Hyper-V virtual disk images (mount offline for full OS access)\n*.vmdk files                      → VMware virtual disk images\n*.bak, *.backup files             → application database backups (may contain credentials)\nSQL database backup files (.bak)  → may restore to extract credentials from app DB\n\n=== MEMORY AND PAGE FILES ===\nC:\\pagefile.sys                   → system page file (may contain memory-resident credentials)\nC:\\hiberfil.sys                   → hibernation file (full memory snapshot — contains credentials)\n%temp%\\*.dmp                      → crash dumps (may contain LSASS memory)\n\n=== SNAFFLER FOR AUTOMATED SWEEP ===\n.\\Snaffler.exe -s -d <domain> -o snaffler.log -v data\nSnaffler specifically targets file extensions and content patterns known to contain credentials\nSearches network shares — finds web.config, connection strings, password files, SSH keys\n\n=== CHAINING CONTEXT ===\n.sav registry files → secretsdump offline → local account hashes without admin tools\nVirtual disk files on backup shares → mount offline → full OS credential access\nhiberfil.sys → volatility/strings extraction → memory-resident credentials\npagefile.sys analysis → find credentials that were swapped to disk\nSCCM logs → deployment account credentials → lateral movement across managed systems",
