      "defense": {
        "prerequisites": "A web application vulnerable to SQL injection (unsanitised user input concatenated into SQL queries). The target parameter must be injectable — SQLMap identifies and confirms this automatically. Network access to the target. For file read/write and OS shell: the DB user must have FILE privilege and secure_file_priv must be empty.",
        "misconfiguration": "Application builds SQL queries by string concatenation with unsanitised input. No WAF or IDS blocks automated SQLi tooling. Error messages returned verbatim exposing DB engine and query structure. No rate-limiting on the vulnerable endpoint — SQLMap's hundreds of requests go unthrottled. DB account has excessive privileges (FILE, DBA).",
        "vulnerable_config": "# PHP — classic vulnerable pattern (the target SQLMap exploits):\n$sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = \" . $_GET[\"id\"] . \" LIMIT 0,1\";\n$result = mysqli_query($link, $sql);\nif (!$result)\n    die(\"<b>SQL error:</b> \" . mysqli_error($link) . \"<br>\");  // exposes error\n\n# DB account with FILE + admin privileges:\nGRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON *.* TO 'webapp'@'localhost';",
        "secure_config": "# Parameterized queries eliminate SQLMap's attack surface:\n$stmt = $conn->prepare('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?');\n$stmt->bind_param('i', $_GET['id']);\n$stmt->execute();\n\n# Least-privilege DB account:\nCREATE USER 'webapp'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'StrongPass!';\nGRANT SELECT ON myapp.items TO 'webapp'@'localhost';\n-- No FILE privilege, no DBA access\n\n# Rate limiting on all POST/GET endpoints:\n# nginx: limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=api:10m rate=30r/m;\n\n# WAF: ModSecurity + OWASP CRS (blocks SQLMap default user-agent + payload signatures)\n# Never expose DB errors — use generic error pages",
        "evasion": "SQLMap's own tamper scripts handle most WAF bypass: randomcase (SeLeCt), space2comment (/**/ replacing spaces), between (NOT BETWEEN), base64encode, percentage encoding. --random-agent swaps the default sqlmap/1.x user-agent (blacklisted by many WAFs). --delay and --safe-freq slow the scan to evade rate-based detection. --proxy routes through Tor or a rotating proxy to hide source IP. --chunk sends chunked HTTP encoding to confuse some WAF parsers. Time-based and error-based techniques avoid UNION signatures entirely.",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M18",
          "MITRE T1190",
          "MITRE T1505.003",
          "OWASP A03:2021",
          "sqlmap GitHub"
        ],
        "why_it_works": "SQLMap's --crawl flag automatically spiders the target web application discovering all forms and injectable parameters. --forms specifically finds and tests HTML form fields. This eliminates the need to manually identify injection points — SQLMap maps the entire application attack surface and tests each discovered parameter.",
        "impact": "Automated full-application SQLi assessment — any form field across the entire site is tested. A single missed input field on an internal admin page can lead to full DB compromise.",
        "detection": "[MITRE T1190] Web crawler pattern: rapid sequential requests to many different URLs on the same host. Many unique POST requests to different endpoints in a short window. Crawler-specific behaviour: requesting robots.txt, sitemap.xml, then following links. Default SQLMap user-agent in logs.",
        "artifacts": "Access log: systematic requests to many pages in sequence (application mapping phase), then targeted payload requests to confirmed forms.",
        "prevention": "robots.txt disallow (minimal protection — tools ignore it). Parameterized queries on all form handlers. Rate limiting per IP. WAF coverage for all form submission endpoints, not just known sensitive ones.",
        "code_review": "RED FLAGS (source): user input concatenated/interpolated into SQL.\n  PHP:    \"...WHERE u='\".$_GET['x'].\"'\"   |  Python: cursor.execute(f\"... {x}\") / % / .format()  |  Node: db.query('...'+req.query.x)\nGREP:  grep -rniE \"(query|execute|prepare)\\(.*(\\$_|req\\.(query|body|params)|f\\\"|%s?\\\"|\\.format)\" .\nSAFE:  parameterized/prepared statements with bound params (?, :name); ORM; least-privilege DB user; no dynamic table/column names from input."
      },
      "type": "command"
