        "why_it_works": "Once SQLMap knows the schema, --dump -T tablename -D dbname runs a SELECT * (or selective column/row) dump of that table via the injection point. Data is returned through the HTTP response (UNION injection) or extracted character-by-character (blind injection). SQLMap automatically identifies and cracks common hash formats in the dumped data.",
