      "notes": "Save the request via Burp 'Copy to file' or right-click 'Save item'. Put * where you want injection, e.g. /?id=* or inside a cookie. Works for JSON bodies too. Use -p to target a specific parameter. Combine with --os-shell --web-root for direct code execution when the DB user has FILE privileges and the web root directory is writable. Also covered in: OSCP PEN-200 Chapter 10 (SQL Injection Attacks).",
