      "name": "SSH - Dynamic Port Forwarding (SOCKS)",
      "command": "ssh -D <socks_port> <user>@<pivot>",
      "description": "Opens a SOCKS proxy over SSH (-D), turning the pivot into a gateway into its internal networks. Point proxychains (or any SOCKS-aware client) at 127.0.0.1:<socks_port> to route tools through the pivot. Add -N -f to background it without a shell.",
