      "examples": [
        {
          "label": "ffuf — match/filter by status, size, words, lines, time",
          "command": "# ffuf\n-mc <code>   match status code\n-fc <code>   filter status code\n-ms <bytes>  match size\n-fs <bytes>  filter size\n-mw <n>      match word count\n-fw <n>      filter word count\n-ml <n>      match line count\n-fl <n>      filter line count\n-mt <ms>     match time (TTFB)"
        },
        {
          "label": "gobuster — status code include/exclude and length",
          "command": "# gobuster (dir mode)\n-s <codes>         include status codes\n-b <codes>         exclude status codes\n--exclude-length   exclude responses of given length"
        },
        {
          "label": "feroxbuster — allowlist/denylist status, size, words, lines, regex",
          "command": "# feroxbuster\n-s / --status-codes    allowlist status codes\n-C / --filter-status   denylist status codes\n-S / --filter-size     filter by size (bytes)\n-W / --filter-words    filter by word count\n-N / --filter-lines    filter by line count\n-X / --filter-regex    filter by body/header regex\n--filter-similar-to    filter near-duplicate pages\n--dont-scan            exclude URLs from scanning"
        },
        {
          "label": "wenum — show/hide by code, length, words, size, regex",
          "command": "# wenum\n--sc   show code        --hc   hide code\n--sl   show lines       --hl   hide lines\n--sw   show words       --hw   hide words\n--ss   show size        --hs   hide size\n--sr   show regex       --hr   hide regex\n--filter       show regex (with plugin processing)\n--hard-filter  hide regex (blocks plugin processing)"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "The key workflow: run a quick scan first, note the most common response size/word-count, then re-run adding -fs or -fw to suppress the noise. ffuf's -ac (auto-calibrate) does this automatically. feroxbuster's --filter-similar-to is best for WAF-deflected responses that all look slightly different.",
