      "defense": {
        "why_it_works": "Dumps LSASS process memory (comsvcs.dll MiniDump, Task Manager, procdump) to a file for offline extraction of cached credentials, hashes, and tickets.",
        "prerequisites": "Local admin/SYSTEM on the Windows target.",
        "impact": "An LSASS minidump containing plaintext creds, NTLM hashes, and Kerberos tickets for offline parsing.",
        "detection": "[MITRE T1003.001] A handle to lsass.exe opened with read/clone rights (Sysmon Event 10; Security 4656/4663 on lsass); known dumper signatures (mimikatz/pypykatz/comsvcs); SYSTEM/debug context preceding it. A new .dmp file on disk is an additional artifact.",
        "artifacts": "An lsass .dmp file; a process opening an lsass handle; the dumper's command line.",
        "prevention": "Enable LSASS protection (RunAsPPL) and Credential Guard; [MITRE T1003 M1026 Privileged Account Management] restrict who reaches SYSTEM/debug; EDR rules on LSASS access; disable WDigest.",
        "evasion": "Direct syscalls / handle-duplication and living-off-the-land (comsvcs.dll) reduce Sysmon-10 fidelity; dump then exfil for offline parsing to avoid running mimikatz on the host.",
        "sources": [
          "HTB M10",
          "MITRE T1003.001"
        ],
        "misconfiguration": "LSASS (Local Security Authority Subsystem Service) runs as a normal Windows process without Virtualization-Based Security (VBS) or Credential Guard. Tools like Mimikatz, ProcDump, or Task Manager can create a full memory dump of LSASS and extract cleartext credentials or NTLM hashes from it. Additionally, WDigest authentication may be enabled (stores cleartext creds in LSASS on older or misconfigured systems).",
        "vulnerable_config": "# WDigest enabled (stores cleartext in LSASS on Windows 7/2008 and older, or if re-enabled):\n# HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\WDigest\n#   UseLogonCredential = 1   <-- BAD: cleartext in LSASS\n\n# No Credential Guard:\n# msinfo32 -> Virtualization-based security Services Running: (none listed)\n\n# No LSA Protection:\n# HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\n#   RunAsPPL = 0  (default on most systems) <-- LSASS not protected process",
        "secure_config": "# 1. Disable WDigest (prevent cleartext in LSASS):\nSet-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\WDigest' \\\n    -Name UseLogonCredential -Value 0\n\n# 2. Enable LSA Protection (PPL — Protected Process Light):\nSet-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa' \\\n    -Name RunAsPPL -Value 1\n# Requires reboot; blocks non-signed tools from reading LSASS memory\n\n# 3. Enable Credential Guard (strongest protection):\n# GPO: Computer Config > Admin Templates > System > Device Guard\n#   'Turn On Virtualization Based Security' = Enabled\n#   'Credential Guard Configuration' = Enabled with UEFI lock\n\n# 4. Add privileged accounts to Protected Users group:\n# Members use Kerberos-only auth — no NTLM, no WDigest, no CredSSP\nAdd-ADGroupMember 'Protected Users' -Members 'Domain Admins','Administrator'"
      },
      "type": "command",
