        "misconfiguration": "User-controlled input rendered into HTML responses without HTML entity encoding (htmlspecialchars() / DOMPurify). No Content Security Policy header. HttpOnly flag absent from session cookies (enables cookie theft via document.cookie). SameSite=None on cookies without Secure. JavaScript frameworks configured to use innerHTML with unsanitised data.",
        "vulnerable_config": "# PHP — raw user input rendered into HTML (stored/reflected XSS):\necho '<div>' . $_POST['comment'] . '</div>';  // No encoding\n// Payload: <script>alert(1)</script> executes on page load\n\n# JavaScript — DOM-based XSS:\nlet task = location.search.split('task=')[1];\ndocument.getElementById('todo').innerHTML = task;  // innerHTML parses HTML\n// Payload in URL: ?task=<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>\n\n# Missing security headers:\n// No Content-Security-Policy header\n// Set-Cookie: session=abc123  (no HttpOnly, no SameSite)",
        "secure_config": "# PHP — always encode output:\necho '<div>' . htmlspecialchars($_POST['comment'], ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8') . '</div>';\n// OR use a templating engine (Twig, Blade) which auto-escapes by default\n\n# JavaScript — use textContent, not innerHTML:\nlet task = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('task');\ndocument.getElementById('todo').textContent = task;  // Never parses HTML\n// OR sanitize with DOMPurify: DOMPurify.sanitize(task)\n\n# Content Security Policy (HTTP header):\nContent-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; object-src 'none';\n// Blocks inline scripts and external script sources\n\n# Secure cookie flags:\nSet-Cookie: session=abc123; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax\n// HttpOnly prevents document.cookie access from JavaScript\n\n# Input validation (defense-in-depth):\n// Allowlist characters for structured inputs (usernames, IDs)\n// Reject or sanitize HTML in free-text fields",
        "prevention": "Output encoding at render time (htmlspecialchars, textContent over innerHTML). Content Security Policy with script-src 'self' blocks inline JS and external script injection. HttpOnly on all session cookies. DOMPurify for rich-text inputs that must allow some HTML. Modern JS frameworks (React, Vue, Angular) escape by default — avoid dangerouslySetInnerHTML. X-XSS-Protection header (legacy browsers). Regular DAST scanning with XSStrike/Burp.",
        "evasion": "Attribute-based payloads bypass tag filters: onerror=, onload=, onfocus=, onmouseover=. Event handlers avoid <script> keyword filtering. Case variation: <ScRiPt>, <SCRIPT>. HTML encoding: &#x3C;script&#x3E;. SVG/MathML contexts: <svg onload=alert(1)>. URL encoding in DOM sinks. Polyglots that work in multiple contexts simultaneously. CSP bypass via JSONP endpoints, open redirects, or CDN script hosts already in the allowlist.",
