        "why_it_works": "The PHP cookie logger receives cookies via GET parameter (?c=), URL-decodes them, and appends each to a creds/cookies.txt file. The attacker hosts this on a local PHP server (php -S 0.0.0.0:80). The XSS payload (script.js with new Image().src=...) is served from the same server — when the victim triggers the stored XSS, their browser loads script.js and exfiltrates document.cookie to index.php.",
